=0\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{x}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $y$ into the second equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-x & =0 \\\\ {(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}-x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-x & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x & =0 \\\\ x(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\text{ }4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $y{:}$\n\n- For $x=0,$ we get $y = \\dfrac{0}{2} = 0.$\n\n- For $x=4,$ we get $y = \\dfrac{4}{2} = 2.$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium points are\n![](images/82/82b6d431638e3abb1c1aebf818f3fbe9f2eb92c7232a3b83c93dc6cb4e563c91.svg)" 13194139534485 17592186045417 false] [17592186311616 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+y(t)+2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)-2y(t)-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of differential equations above?" 13194139534485 17592186045417 true] [17592186311616 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+y(t)+2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)-2y(t)-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of differential equations above?" 13194139534485 17592186045417 false] [17592186311616 1074 "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2=0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2y-4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+2=0\\,⇒\\,y=-x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $y$ into the second equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2y-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2(-x-2)-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+4-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x & =0 \\\\ x(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\text{ }0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $y:$\n\n- For $x=0,$ we get $y=-0-2=-2.$\n\n- For $x=-2,$ we get $y=-(-2)-2=0.$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium points are\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534485 17592186045417 true] [17592186311616 1074 "The equilibrium (fixed) points of 